NDIP-3 A2 negative-origin and wrapped nanoTime regression
Date: 2026-10-01
Base commit: 5c2f50fd6a0dfc25e7a878b43a5a19bd41b9dd68

Contract basis:
  Java SE System.nanoTime documentation says readings use an arbitrary origin,
  may be negative, and elapsed time must be computed by subtracting readings.
  https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/System.html#nanoTime()

Change:
  BoundedReadBudget no longer rejects negative clock readings or compares
  absolute signed values. It checks forward progress using modular elapsed
  deltas, which accepts a valid signed-long wrap while still rejecting a
  backward step within the observed interval.

